# Data files
#
# ANCHORED to the repo root on purpose. A bare `data/` matches at ANY depth,
# which silently swallowed `services/drift/app/data/` — 11 source modules the
# drift service imports at runtime (forcing_factory, cmems_provider, era5_loader,
# gfs_provider, mock_forcing, ...). They were never committed, so a fresh clone
# could not import the forcing layer at all and `pytest` died during collection
# with ModuleNotFoundError. Runtime data lives at the root; source code does not.
/data/
/services/data/
# The extension rules below still catch stray data files anywhere in the tree,
# which is what actually keeps large binaries out of the history.
*.csv
*.geojson
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.prj
*.tif
*.tiff
*.nc
*.hdf5
*.h5

